  "notes": "{後|あと}ずさる describes stepping backward, typically as an instinctive reaction to fear, surprise, or discomfort.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{後|あと}ずさっている indicates the person is in the process of backing away.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {思|おも}わず{後|あと}ずさる: to involuntarily step back\n- じりじりと{後|あと}ずさる: to gradually back away\n- {後|あと}ずさりする: to back away (noun + する form)\n\nFORMS:\n- Noun form: {後|あと}ずさり\n- Variant: {後|あと}じさる (dialectal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {退|しりぞ}く: to retreat (more formal, deliberate or strategic)\n- {引|ひ}き{下|さ}がる: to withdraw, to back down",
